# Directus SDK client (read-only)

One client in `config/directus.ts`: `createDirectus<Schema>(url).with(staticToken).with(rest())`. Schema generic is required. URL = `NEXT_PUBLIC_DIRECTUS_URL`. Token = `DIRECTUS_STATIC_TOKEN`. Never `?access_token=`. No second client / `graphql()` unless explicitly requested.

Fetch with `directus.request(readItems | readItem | readSingleton | ...)`. Never `ofetch`/`fetch` to `/items/*` (ofetch is only `globals.fetch` on the client). Custom paths: `customEndpoint<OutputType>({ path, method })`.

Catch API errors with `isDirectusError(error)`. This frontend is read-only: never `createItems` / `updateItems` / `deleteItems` / nested `{ create, update, delete }`. Writes live in Directus Studio.

Install with **pnpm** only (`pnpm add @directus/sdk`). Never npm/npx.

```ts
// BAD
await fetch(`${url}/items/pages?access_token=...`)
await directus.request(createItems("pages", [...]))

// GOOD
await directus.request(readItems("pages", query))
catch (e) { if (isDirectusError(e)) ... }
```
